    <item>
      <title>Definitive First Person View</title>
      <author>bubbabushido</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/720730</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/720730#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">a4d94035758c4e733ccd73ba60a321f285339c23</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 18:58:52 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab6d26d25e9a.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab778791ecd6.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab778794a048.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ab778798501c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Definitive First Person&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Change&lt;/em&gt;: Flower shrine fix (and probably others)&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;# BOTW First Person v1.6.1&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;First-person gameplay for The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild on Cemu, with an animated eye-level camera, visible player and equipment, enemy lock-on, and a custom stamina HUD.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Features&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Animated eye-position camera, 8 cm forward offset, and 90° horizontal FOV at 16:9 (approximately 58.7° vertical).&lt;br&gt;- Visible body and equipment, with head-material visibility controlled by the active scene camera and event state.&lt;br&gt;- Shield guard pose tuned for first person: the shield sits in front of you and stays visible while guarding; Link's head and its shadow stay intact.&lt;br&gt;- Paraglider is visible while gliding; upward view is limited to 60° while gliding.&lt;br&gt;- Riding a horse or the Master Cycle raises the eye 5 cm and moves it 10 cm back, and limits the downward view to 30°, so the mount's neck and body don't clip into the view.&lt;br&gt;- First-person camera collision: the eye is kept 15 cm in front of walls, boulders and other solid geometry, using the game's own camera collision layers.&lt;br&gt;- The eye stays above water surfaces, so diving and splashing in no longer show the view from under the water.&lt;br&gt;- While guarding, the main camera uses a 6 cm near clip so the shield stays visible; at all other times the native near clip is kept, avoiding distant shadow flicker.&lt;br&gt;- Camera pulls back 10 cm while pushing boulders.&lt;br&gt;- Nearby objects no longer fade out near the first-person camera (e.g. the cooking pot while holding ingredients).&lt;br&gt;- Cooking prompt works while looking at the pot: its activation fan is widened from 45° to 90°, since turning the view in first person doesn't turn Link's body.&lt;br&gt;- Body yaw follows the view during ordinary movement. Climbing retains native body orientation and animation.&lt;br&gt;- Native enemy lock-on with first-person eye placement.&lt;br&gt;- Native bow-arm animation with the original 20° stance alignment and an 8 cm camera-right aiming-body offset, keeping hand and bow together.&lt;br&gt;- Stamina wheel beside the hearts, at 75% scale; approximately 7.5 screen pixels from the leftmost heart at 1920×1080. Gap scales with HUD resolution. Original-position preset also available.&lt;br&gt;- Sheikah Slate camera/scope adjustments; fixed-FOV first-person bow cameras without bow zoom.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Changes in v1.6.1&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Fixes scripted events that wait for a talk camera to finish and never continued, e.g. stepping on Magda's flowers in the *Watch Out for the Flowers* shrine quest: the second dialogue never started and the game soft-locked. The original FPV camera AI replaced the game's talk cameras with the free player camera, which never reports finishing.&lt;br&gt;- The automatic talk cameras (`CameraEventTalk`, actions 12–15) and the manual talk cameras (`CameraEventTalkManualCtrl` / `…Ret`, actions 34–37) use the game's own classes again, at the same positions, so every other camera index used by this pack is unchanged.&lt;br&gt;- Talk scenes stay in first person: the eye camera is applied at the end of both talk camera classes' updates, the same way the enemy lock-on camera is handled.&lt;br&gt;- A scan of all 997 event packs found the waiting camera steps that could reach those cameras (`Demo_Talk`, `Demo_ReturnSavePoint_1`, `Demo_LookStone`); they now use the restored classes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Changes in v1.6.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Paraglider is now visible in first person (it was faded out like other attached items), and the upward view is limited to 60° while gliding.&lt;br&gt;- Mounts: while riding a horse or the Master Cycle the eye is raised 5 cm and pulled back 10 cm, and the downward view is limited to 30°, preventing the camera from clipping into the mount when running fast or uphill.&lt;br&gt;- Guarding no longer shifts the body forward (that put Link's hair into view), and the guard near clip is 6 cm so the shield's nearest edge isn't cut.&lt;br&gt;- Link's head is no longer hidden, so his shadow keeps its head; the native near clip keeps the head out of the first-person view.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Changes in v1.5.3&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- The cooking pot (and other objects) no longer fade out when close to the first-person camera, e.g. while holding ingredients at a pot.&lt;br&gt;- The Cook prompt's activation fan is widened from 45° to 90° for all cooking pots (`Item_CookSet`, `Item_CookSet_100enemy`, `Item_CookSet_PanOnly`), because in first person you look at the pot without Link's body facing it. Only that value is changed in these actor packs; file sizes are unchanged.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Changes in v1.5.2&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- In-engine cutscenes and talk scenes stay in first person with the view locked level to Link's facing; the view no longer ends up disconnected or reversed after camera cuts (e.g. entering a shrine).&lt;br&gt;- Link's shadow keeps its head: head materials are only hidden while guarding.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Changes in v1.5.1&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Fixes the graphic pack's location in Cemu's list: it now appears under **Mods → First Person View**. Earlier versions placed it inside the official BotW Graphics pack's entry, which conflicts with that pack. After updating, enable it again under Mods.&lt;br&gt;- Updated pack name and in-game description.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Changes in v1.5.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Adds first-person camera collision: a ray from Link's body to the eye (game camera collision layers) keeps the view 15 cm in front of solid surfaces such as boulders and walls.&lt;br&gt;- Adds a water-surface clamp: a vertical water-only ray keeps the eye 10 cm above the surface, including deep plunges when diving in from a height.&lt;br&gt;- The lowered near clip now applies only while guarding (and only to the main camera), fixing flickering distant shadows caused by reduced depth precision.&lt;br&gt;- Adds tunables for collision margin, water margin and ray height, and near-clip scope in `patch_Live.asm`.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Changes in v1.4.1&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Fixes an intermittent wrong bow angle on draw (often after crouching or turning) that corrected itself on redraw. The aiming stance no longer samples the body's animated rotation at the start of the draw; it always uses the settled aim stance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Changes in v1.4.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Fixes the shield disappearing (or only appearing when looking down) while guarding. The cause was the game's dynamic near clip plane (about 0.7–1.0 m); the main first-person camera now uses 10 cm. Shadows and other cameras keep their native values.&lt;br&gt;- Fixes seeing through boulders and other close objects for the same reason.&lt;br&gt;- Guarding shifts the body 10 cm forward along the view, keeping hand and shield together; the camera stays in place.&lt;br&gt;- Fixed left-arm guard pose (from the game's own shield-guard animation) for a stable shield position.&lt;br&gt;- Equipped items (weapons, shield, bow, nocked arrow) skip the frustum-plane stage of the game's per-model view culling while in first person, avoiding pop-out at screen edges near the camera.&lt;br&gt;- 10 cm camera pull-back while pushing boulders.&lt;br&gt;- Tunable values are grouped in `patch_Live.asm` with documented offsets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Compatibility&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tested on **Cemu 2.6, Ubuntu, Wii U EUR BOTW v208**.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Title ID: `00050000101C9500`&lt;br&gt;- Executable module hash: `0x6267BFD0`&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This package targets that version and region. Other versions/regions and operating systems have not been verified. No mod manager or BetterVR runtime is required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Install or update&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Close Cemu.&lt;br&gt;2. Back up and remove any older `00_FirstPersonView_ZoomFix` folder from Cemu's `graphicPacks` directory.&lt;br&gt;3. Extract this ZIP and copy its `00_FirstPersonView_ZoomFix` folder into `graphicPacks`.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;On the tested Linux setup: `~/.local/share/Cemu/graphicPacks/`.&lt;br&gt;4. Enable **The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild → Mods → First Person View** in Cemu's Graphic Packs settings.&lt;br&gt;5. Select **Beside hearts** for the custom stamina position and launch BOTW.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Use only one copy of this pack. Disable other camera replacements and stamina-position patches that modify the same features. Restart the game after updating the files.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;To uninstall, disable this graphic pack and restart Cemu.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Notes&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Shield visibility while guarding, the bow-draw angle fix, camera collision against boulders, diving/water behaviour and the absence of distant shadow flicker outside guarding were confirmed in gameplay on the tested setup. Collision is much improved but not perfect in every situation. The v1.6.1 Magda fix (automatic talk cameras) was confirmed in gameplay; the manual talk camera change has not yet been exercised in gameplay. Hair visibility in the guard pose, real-time cutscenes, climbing view limits, and full-game/outfit coverage have not been fully verified; clipping or camera edge cases may remain.&amp;nbsp; While guarding, the lowered near clip reduces depth precision and distant shadows may flicker.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Native arrow firing and gameplay logic remain in control of the game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Texture upscales, lighting mods, shaders, controller profiles, streaming automation, emulator, and full game files are not included. This is not stereoscopic VR output.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;## Credits and notices&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Original First Person View: **MelonSpeedruns, SushiiZ, and SilentVerge**. Original attribution README included as `README-original-FPV.txt`; its three-FOV-variant description refers to the original release.&lt;br&gt;- Native body/camera and equipment work uses layout research and hook techniques from **Crementif's BotW-BetterVR**. Its MIT notice is included as `LICENSE-BetterVR.txt`.&lt;br&gt;- Stamina implementation used Cemu community graphic-pack GUI/aspect-ratio patches as a reference.&lt;br&gt;- The fixed guard-arm rotations are frame-0 values derived from the game's own `Shield_Guard_Wait` animation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The original FPV archive did not include a separate license. Attribution and the BetterVR notice are preserved; no blanket license is asserted over third-party or game-derived material. Redistribution permission for those components has not been independently verified.</description>
